 2. 🇺🇦 Trump demands new Ukraine leader 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 


 President Trump talks to reporters as he leaves the White House for Clarksville, Tenn., yesterday. Photo: Aaron Schwartz/Getty Images President Trump called yesterday for Ukraine to replace President Volodymyr Zelensky with someone willing to make a deal with Russia to end the war.

 Why it matters: Trump's attack on Zelensky, which came after the Ukrainian president criticized his diesel deal with Russia , signals the most serious crisis between the two leaders since their February 2025 meeting exploded in front of cameras, Axios' Barak Ravid reports. 👀 Trump said Zelensky could have reached a deal with Russia many times "but chooses not to."

 "I suggest they get a new leader who can make a deal," Trump told reporters yesterday. "… And I think it's time for Ukraine to get a new president." He said he asked Zelensky to stop attacking Russian oil refineries and claimed Zelensky's actions harmed American farmers.

 "He better damn well stop," Trump said. 🏛️ What we're watching: Rep. Brian Fitzpatrick (R-Pa.) vowed yesterday to force a House vote to block Russian oil purchases, challenging the diesel deal, Axios' Andrew Solender and Andrew Pantazi report. 

 Fitzpatrick, co-chair of the Congressional Ukraine Caucus, said he would introduce the "Ronald Reagan Peace Through Strength Act" and force a vote through a discharge petition. Share this story . 

 
 
