 5. ✨ Nvidia&#x27;s AI shopping spree 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Mike Tannenbaum, of Fairfax, Va., takes a selfie with Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang before President Trump's science summit at the U.S. Institute of Peace on Thursday. Photo: Jacquelyn Martin/AP Nvidia is in early talks to buy or expand its investment in Reflection AI , an American startup developing open-weight AI models to compete with cheap Chinese systems, the Financial Times reports. 

 Why it matters: Nvidia has been on an investment blitz, pouring billions into the AI industry to boost it and cement its place at the center of it. The intrigue: " [A] deal could take a number of shapes, including a so-called 'acqui-hire' where Nvidia would hire staff and license technology without the drawn-out regulatory review that comes with a full acquisition," FT reports. 

 "Acqui-hires have become increasingly popular among Big Tech companies looking to avoid antitrust scrutiny of AI dealmaking." Read on (gift link). 

 
 
