 6. 🕊️ Pope Leo to undergo lung surgery 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Pope Leo waves from the window of the Apostolic Palace overlooking St. Peter's Square in the Vatican today. Photo: Filippo Monteforte/AFP via Getty Images Pope Leo said today that tests have discovered a nodule in his lung , which he will have removed surgically this week: 

 "Dear friends, during some recent medical examinations, doctors found a localized nodule in my lung. It was detected at a very early stage and is well localized. The doctors believe surgery is appropriate. Following their advice, I have therefore decided to undergo an operation to remove it. The operation is already scheduled for the coming days. I thank you for your spiritual closeness and entrust myself to your prayers." The big picture: The first American pontiff, age 71, is less than 18 months into a papacy that has been defined by public stances at odds with the White House , including clashes over immigration and deep skepticism about AI, Axios' Ben Berkowitz reports. 

 The pope didn't say if the nodule was malignant. Vatican officials said the operation would be in the next few days, and the recovery would take about a week. Share this story . 

 
 
