 John Mateer, quarterback for the Oklahoma Sooners, celebrates on top of the Sooner Schooner after defeating the Texas Longhorns in Dallas yesterday. Photo: Gunnar Word/Getty Images Stunning upset on one of college football's biggest stages: Yesterday, for the first time ever, Oklahoma beat a No. 1 Texas team in the storied Red River Rivalry.

 The Sooners picked off Longhorns quarterback Arch Manning with 19 seconds left. Oklahoma's Tate Sandell kicked a 47-yard field goal for the W. Watch a clip . 

 
 
